export anchor DBAdminStyle:
    number: 404
    screen: DatabaseConsole
    name: DB admin
    idea: A professional dark console built from square ruled panes, a tree, a tabbed editor and a dense grid, where a single cyan accent marks only what runs and what is selected.
    base: dark
    palette:
        page: #111418, the frame and gaps between panes
        pane: #181c21, the schema tree, results grid, history and style sheet
        head: #20252c, pane headers, the toolbar, grid headers and row numbers
        well: #0c0e11, the editor, the title bar, fields and the status bar
        line: #2c333c, every rule between panes, rows and cells
        ink: #e2e6ea, text
        muted: #9aa4b0, column types, line numbers, meta and pane titles
        accent: #5cc8d6, the Run button, the active tab stripe, function names and focus
        onAccent: #062227, text on the accent
        accentSoft: #163037, the selected tree row and the current grid row
        keyword: #c6a8ff, SQL keywords
        number: #f2c879, numbers, primary key icons and the Read-only label
        ok: #7fd9a0, Succeeded and string literals
        bad: #ff9c94, Failed and the error message, on #2a1719
    type:
        System sans, system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica Neue, Arial, for
        chrome at 13px and 1.45. Data uses ui-monospace, SF Mono, Menlo,
        Consolas. Pane titles are 11px bold caps with 0.06em tracking. The
        editor is 13px mono at 1.6, the grid and tree 12px mono. The app
        name is 13px at 600.
    layout:
        A desktop database tool. A 36px title bar holds a cyan B square,
        Brightwork Data, a bordered production-replica chip with a cylinder
        icon and an amber padlock Read-only on the far right. Below sits a
        toolbar with Run in cyan with its shortcut, then Format, Save, a
        divider and Explain. The workspace is three columns. A 240px schema
        tree shows production-replica, then the five tables with chevrons,
        tasks opened and tinted, and its six columns with key icons for id,
        project_id and assignee_id and types right aligned. The centre has
        two file tabs, the active one with a cyan top stripe, a line
        numbered editor with coloured SQL, a green Succeeded bar with 3 rows
        and 38 ms, then a ruled grid with row numbers, typed column headers
        and right aligned amber counts. A 260px History pane lists three
        runs with time, name, duration and a tick or cross line, the failed
        one with a red edged error box. A segmented status bar closes the
        screen. Below 1100px History drops under the grid. Below 720px every
        pane stacks and the grid scrolls inside itself.
    spacing: A 4px unit. 28px pane headers, 5px by 10px grid cells, 8px by 10px history rows.
    density: High. Tree, editor, grid and history are all visible at once.
    corners: 2px on buttons, fields and chips. Panes and the grid are square.
    borders: 1px #2c333c rules between every pane, row and cell. The style sheet starts with a 4px cyan top rule.
    shadows: None. Depth comes from four surface steps.
    icons:
        14px square capped line icons at 1.6 stroke. Cylinder for the
        database, ruled box for tables, a key for key columns, a dash for
        plain columns, tick for Succeeded and cross for Failed, each beside
        its word.
    focus: A 2px cyan outline inset 2px on controls, rows and fields, offset outward on the Run button.
    tone: Terse tool labels, such as Run, Format, Explain, Succeeded and 3 rows.
